<title>HONG KONG: MASCargo said planning Macau 737F service.</title>
<headline>MASCargo said planning Macau 737F service.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>MASKargo is planning to start a freighter service to Macau at end-October, probably using a Boeing 737, industry sources told Reuters.</p>
<p>MASKargo is part of the Malaysian Airline System Bhd group and operates both Boeing 737-500 and 737-300 freighters.</p>
<p>A MASKargo spokesman speaking from Kuala Lumpur said he could not comment in detail but added: &quot;Our plan to introduce freighter services to Macau has yet to be finalised. --Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 8982 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
